
// Nested IFs
// Max Score: 2 | Difficulty: Not Specified
// Nested IFs happen when we put an IF statement inside an IF statement.

// The pseudocode looks like this:

// IF <condition> Then
//   IF <condition> THEN
//     //code
//   END IF
//   //code
// END IF
// You can nest as many IFs as you want, but it is good practice to limit them to 3 or 4, or else they become difficult to read.

// For this challenge, convert the pseudocode below into Java:

// INPUT a number
// INPUT a string
// CHECK if the number is even
// IF it is, CHECK if the string length is even
// IF it is, OUTPUT "string length is even"
// ELSE, OUTPUT "string length is odd"
// Then OUTPUT "the number is even"
// IF the number is odd, OUTPUT "the number is odd"
// The expected input is:
// An integer
// A string
// e.g. 6
// "Smell my cheese"
// The expected output is:
// string length is odd
// The number is even
DECLARE num:INTEGER
DECLARE str:STRING
INPUT num
INPUT str
IF MOD(num,2)=0 THEN 
    IF MOD(LENGTH(str),2)=0 THEN
        OUTPUT  "string length is even"
    ELSE
        OUTPUT "string length is odd"
    ENDIF
    OUTPUT "the number is even"
ELSE 
    IF MOD(LENGTH(str),2)=0 THEN
        OUTPUT  "string length is even"
    ELSE
        OUTPUT "string length is odd"
    ENDIF
    OUTPUT "the number is odd"
ENDIF
